# JSDoc Comments on Exported Declarations

The SDK reference docs are auto-generated from JSDoc comments by `scripts/generate-api-docs.ts`. Single-line `//` comments are invisible to the extraction script.

## Rule

Use `/** JSDoc */` comments (not `//`) on:

- Exported interface/type properties
- Exported type aliases
- Exported function/method signatures
- Interface member descriptions inside event maps

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — invisible to docs generation
export interface PanelConfig {
  // Panel width in pixels
  width?: number;
}

// ✅ GOOD — extracted into API reference docs
export interface PanelConfig {
  /** Panel width in pixels. @default 380 */
  width?: number;
}
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — type alias with no JSDoc
export type PanelMode = 'overlay' | 'push';

// ✅ GOOD
/** How the panel interacts with page content. */
export type PanelMode = 'overlay' | 'push';
```

`//` comments are fine inside function bodies for implementation notes.

## Regenerating Docs

After adding or changing JSDoc, run:

```bash
npx tsx scripts/generate-api-docs.ts
```

This updates `frontend/generated/api-types.json` and `frontend/examples/generated/*.ts.txt`.
